# Education Specific AI Tools

#### Some tools are specifically designed for educational settings and may better align with school requirements. These tools can provide a safer entry point for integrating AI directly into classrooms.

#### When looking for student-friendly AI tools, look for ones that:
* #### Prioritize student privacy
* #### Offer teacher controls or dashboards
* #### Focus on learning support rather than answer-giving

#### Below are a few examples of AI tools developed specificaly for educational use. If you are interested, click on the logo to learn more. 

<br>

<div style="text-align: center; width: 80%; margin: 0 auto;">
  <p style="
    font-size: 18px; 
    background-color: #F5F7F8; 
    padding: 10px; 
    border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; 
    border-right: 5px solid #8148B2;
    display: inline-block;
  "><strong>Important Disclaimer</strong> <br><br>Just because a tool was designed specifically for educational use does not mean it's okay to use in your school or classroom. <br><br><strong>When in doubt always follow school and district guidelines.</strong>
  </p>
</div>

<br>

